**Week 1 Common Mistakes:**

**1. Variable Declaration Mistakes**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Not initialized
int number;
System.out.println(number);  // Compilation error!

// ✅ CORRECT - Initialize before use
int number = 0;
System.out.println(number);  // 0
```

**2. Integer Division**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Integer division truncates
int avg = 10 / 3;  // 3 (not 3.33...)

// ✅ CORRECT - Cast to double
double avg = (double) 10 / 3;  // 3.333...
```

**3. Comparison vs Assignment**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Assignment, not comparison
if (x = 5) {  // Compilation error!
    // ...
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use ==
if (x == 5) {
    // ...
}
```

**4. Off-by-One in Loops**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Includes arr.length
for (int i = 0; i <= arr.length; i++) {
    System.out.println(arr[i]);  // Crashes!
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use <
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    System.out.println(arr[i]);
}
```

**5. Array Length vs String length()**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Mixing up property and method
int[] arr = {1, 2, 3};
int size = arr.length();  // Error! No parentheses

String text = "Hello";
int len = text.length;    // Error! Need parentheses

// ✅ CORRECT
int size = arr.length;     // Property
int len = text.length();   // Method
```

**6. Shallow Copy**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Shallow copy
int[] arr1 = {1, 2, 3};
int[] arr2 = arr1;  // Same array!
arr2[0] = 100;      // Changes arr1 too

// ✅ CORRECT - Deep copy
int[] arr2 = arr1.clone();
arr2[0] = 100;  // Doesn't affect arr1
```

**7. Missing break in switch**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Fall-through
switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");  // Prints both!
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Add break
switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");
        break;
}
```

**8. Infinite Loops**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Forgot to increment
int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    System.out.println(i);
    // Forgot i++!
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Update counter
int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;
}
```

**9. Modifying Array in for-each**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Doesn't modify array
for (int num : arr) {
    num = num * 2;  // Only modifies copy!
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use indexed loop
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    arr[i] = arr[i] * 2;
}
```

**10. Wrong Initial Value for Max/Min**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Assumes max >= 0
int[] arr = {-5, -10, -3};
int max = 0;  // Wrong! All numbers negative

// ✅ CORRECT - Use first element
int max = arr[0];  // -5, then finds -3
```

**Prevention Checklist:**
- ✅ Initialize variables before use
- ✅ Cast for decimal division
- ✅ Use == for comparison, = for assignment
- ✅ Loop with i < length, not i <= length
