**2. Matrix Multiplication Dimension Check:**

**Requirements:**
- Matrix1 columns must equal Matrix2 rows
- Result dimensions: [m1.rows][m2.cols]

**Dimension Rules:**
```
Matrix A [m × n] × Matrix B [n × p] = Result [m × p]

Examples:
[2×3] × [3×4] = [2×4] ✅ Valid (3 == 3)
[3×2] × [3×4] = ERROR  ❌ Invalid (2 != 3)
[4×3] × [3×2] = [4×2] ✅ Valid (3 == 3)
```

```java
public class MatrixMultiplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] m1 = {
            {1, 2, 3},
            {4, 5, 6}
        };  // 2×3

        int[][] m2 = {
            {7, 8},
            {9, 10},
            {11, 12}
        };  // 3×2

        int[][] result = multiplyMatrices(m1, m2);

        if (result != null) {
            System.out.println("Result matrix:");
            printMatrix(result);
        }
    }

    public static int[][] multiplyMatrices(int[][] m1, int[][] m2) {
        // Check if multiplication is possible
        if (m1[0].length != m2.length) {
            System.out.println("Error: Cannot multiply matrices");
            System.out.println("Matrix1 columns (" + m1[0].length + 
                ") must equal Matrix2 rows (" + m2.length + ")");
            return null;
        }

        int m1Rows = m1.length;
        int m1Cols = m1[0].length;
        int m2Cols = m2[0].length;

        int[][] result = new int[m1Rows][m2Cols];

        // Multiply
        for (int i = 0; i < m1Rows; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < m2Cols; j++) {
                for (int k = 0; k < m1Cols; k++) {
                    result[i][j] += m1[i][k] * m2[k][j];
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void printMatrix(int[][] matrix) {
        for (int[] row : matrix) {
            for (int val : row) {
                System.out.print(val + "\t");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```
Result matrix:
58   64
139  154
```

**Calculation Example:**
```
Result[0][0] = (1×7) + (2×9) + (3×11) = 7 + 18 + 33 = 58
Result[0][1] = (1×8) + (2×10) + (3×12) = 8 + 20 + 36 = 64
Result[1][0] = (4×7) + (5×9) + (6×11) = 28 + 45 + 66 = 139
Result[1][1] = (4×8) + (5×10) + (6×12) = 32 + 50 + 72 = 154
```

**Key Points:**

**Addition:**
- Same dimensions required
- Add corresponding elements: result[i][j] = m1[i][j] + m2[i][j]
- Result has same dimensions as inputs

**Multiplication:**
- m1.columns must equal m2.rows
- Triple nested loop required
- Result dimensions: [m1.rows][m2.cols]

